@* The switch that reveals every Arabic gloss in the dashboard at once.

   Rendered once by _DashboardLayout, so it governs the whole shell — sidebar, page
   headings, table headers — rather than one page's labels. A visitor either reads the
   dashboard in Arabic or they do not, and a switch per label would be a dozen ways to
   get the same setting wrong.

   The behaviour lives in wwwroot/js/translations.js; only markup here. The matching boot
   script is inline in _DashboardLayout's <head>, because the glosses are hidden by CSS and
   the preference has to be on <html> before anything renders — a network round trip would
   be too late, and a page saved with translations on would flash French-only first.

   Both captions ship in the markup and CSS picks between them, so the script's only job is
   to flip an attribute and remember the choice. *@
<button type="button"
        class="tr-toggle"
        data-tr-toggle
        aria-pressed="false"
        aria-label="Ajouter la traduction arabe des libellés"
        title="Ajouter la traduction arabe des libellés">
    <partial name="Icons/Translate" />
    <span class="tr-toggle-txt">
        <span data-tr-caption="off">Traduction</span>
        <span data-tr-caption="on">Masquer</span>
    </span>
</button>